  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/vaginitis/conditioninfo/complications",
    "title": "Can vaginitis lead to other health problems? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Breadcrumb",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Without treatment, symptoms of vaginitis can worsen. Some types of vaginitis can increase a woman's risk of other health problems.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/vaginitis/conditioninfo/complications",
    "title": "Can vaginitis lead to other health problems? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Breadcrumb",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Bacterial vaginosis (BV) increases a woman's risk of getting other sexually transmitted diseases, including HIV, if she is exposed to the pathogens that cause them.1 BV also is associated with pelvic inflammatory disease, a serious disease that can harm a woman's reproductive organs and cause infertility.1 Having BV increases a woman's risk of preterm labor and preterm birth. Women who have it also are more likely to get an infection after having surgery such as a hysterectomy.1",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/vaginitis/conditioninfo/complications",
    "title": "Can vaginitis lead to other health problems? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Breadcrumb",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Trichomoniasis increases a woman's risk of getting or spreading other sexually transmitted diseases such as HIV.2 Trichomoniasis also may cause preterm labor or preterm birth.2",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
