  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo",
    "title": "About Pre-Pregnancy Care and Prenatal Care | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "What is pre-pregnancy care?",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Pre-Pregnancy care is the health care a woman receives before she gets pregnant to help promote a healthy pregnancy.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo",
    "title": "About Pre-Pregnancy Care and Prenatal Care | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "What is pre-pregnancy care?",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Taking steps to make sure you are healthy and avoiding exposure to harmful behaviors and toxins before you get pregnant can decrease the chance of problems during pregnancy and improve the health of your child.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo",
    "title": "About Pre-Pregnancy Care and Prenatal Care | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "What is prenatal care?",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Prenatal care is the health care a woman gets during pregnancy. Prenatal care should begin as soon as a woman knows or thinks she is pregnant. Early and regular prenatal visits are important for the health of both the mother and the fetus.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo",
    "title": "About Pre-Pregnancy Care and Prenatal Care | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "What is prenatal care?",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Research shows that prenatal care makes a difference for a healthy pregnancy. Women who do not seek prenatal care are three times as likely to deliver a low birth weight infant. Lack of prenatal care can also increase the risk of infant death.1",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo",
    "title": "About Pre-Pregnancy Care and Prenatal Care | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Citations",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Womenshealth.gov. (2009, March 6). Publications: Prenatal care fact sheet. Retrieved April 12, 2012, from http://www.womenshealth.gov/publications/our-publications/fact-sheet/prenatal-care.html",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Breadcrumb",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "For women who are thinking about getting pregnant, following a health care provider's advice can reduce the risk of problems during pregnancy and after birth. A health care provider can recommend ways to get the proper nutrition and avoid habits that can have lasting harmful effects on a fetus.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Breadcrumb",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "For example, taking a supplement containing at least 400 micrograms of folic acid before getting pregnant can reduce the risk of complications such as neural tube defects (NTDs)—abnormalities that can occur in the brain, spine, or spinal column of a developing fetus and are present at birth.1,2",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Breadcrumb",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "A pre-pregnancy care visit with your health care provider can improve the chances of a healthy pregnancy. A health care provider will likely recommend that you do the following:",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Develop a plan for your reproductive life.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "This plan includes your and your partner’s plans for the number and timing of pregnancies based on your values and life goals. Sharing your life plan with your health care provider can help address any potential problems before you conceive.2",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Adopt a healthy diet and lifestyle.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "You can reduce the chance that you will be diagnosed with gestational diabetes (high blood sugar diagnosed during pregnancy) by taking steps to improve your diet and lifestyle before you get pregnant. Gestational diabetes can increase the risk to your health as well as your infant's. In addition, pre-pregnancy exercise is also associated with lower risk for gestational diabetes, and the benefit increases with more vigorous levels of exercise.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Adopt a healthy diet and lifestyle.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Here are some specific dietary suggestions for women who are planning for a pregnancy:3,4,5,6",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Adopt a healthy diet and lifestyle.",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Increase your intake of fiber. Eating 10 more grams of fiber in the form of cereals, fruits, and vegetables is associated with 26% lower risk of gestational diabetes.18",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Adopt a healthy diet and lifestyle.",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Reduce consumption of sugar-sweetened cola. Women who drank five or more such beverages per week before they got pregnant were at greater risk of gestational diabetes.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Adopt a healthy diet and lifestyle.",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Eat less red meat, processed meats, and animal fats and cholesterol. Eating less of these foods before pregnancy can decrease the chances of developing diabetes when you are pregnant.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Adopt a healthy diet and lifestyle.",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Replace animal protein with protein from nuts to lower your risk of gestational diabetes. Studies have shown that substituting vegetable protein for animal protein before pregnancy can decrease risk of gestational diabetes by about half.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Increase your intake of folic acid.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Folic acid is a B vitamin (B9). It helps produce and maintain new cells.7 This is especially important during times when the cells are dividing and growing rapidly such as infancy and pregnancy.8",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Increase your intake of folic acid.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "The United States Public Health Service recommends that all pregnant women and “women of childbearing age [15 to 44 years] in the United States who are capable of becoming pregnant should consume [a supplement containing] 0.4 mg of folic acid per day for the purpose of reducing their risk of having a pregnancy affected with spina bifida or other NTDs.” 9",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Increase your intake of folic acid.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Although a related form of folic acid (called folate) is present in orange juice and leafy, green vegetables (such as kale and spinach), folate is not absorbed as well as folic acid.10 Studies show that taking folic acid for 3 months before getting pregnant and for 3 months after conceiving can reduce the risk of NTDs such as spina bifida 11,12 by up to 70%.13",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Get up to date on vaccines.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Ask your health care provider if you need a booster for any vaccines. Some vaccines can be given during pregnancy, but the rubella (German measles) and varicella (chicken pox) vaccines are recommended before you get pregnant.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Get up to date on vaccines.",
    "tag": "h2",
    "text": "Talk to your health care provider about your diabetes or other medical conditions.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Talk to your health care provider about your diabetes or other medical conditions.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Many health problems affect not only the pregnant woman but also the developing infant. Some examples are diabetes, hypertension (high blood pressure), infections, asthma, seizure disorders, and maternal phenylketonuria (an inherited condition in which the pregnant woman’s body can’t break down the amino acid phenylalanine [pronounced fen-l-AL-uh-neen], resulting in high levels in her blood). Getting health problems under control before and during pregnancy reduces the risk of miscarriage and stillbirth as well as other health problems for the infant.11",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Avoid smoking, drinking alcohol, and taking drugs.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "During pregnancy, these behaviors can increase the risk for sudden infant death syndrome (SIDS), preterm birth, fetal alcohol spectrum disorders, and NTDs.14 If you are trying to quit smoking, drinking, or doing drugs and you need help, talk to your health care provider about support groups or about medications.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Avoid smoking, drinking alcohol, and taking drugs.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Advice, tips, and support to help women quit smoking (including expecting mothers) are available through the Smokefree Women website.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Strive to reach a healthy weight before trying to get pregnant.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Obesity may make it more difficult to become pregnant.15 Having overweight or obesity also puts you at risk for complications during pregnancy, such as high blood pressure, preeclampsia, gestational diabetes, and stillbirth, and increases the chances of cesarean delivery.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Strive to reach a healthy weight before trying to get pregnant.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "NICHD researchers have found that obesity can increase your child’s risk of a congenital heart defect (a problem with the heart that is present at birth) by 15%.16 Research has also uncovered a link between obesity and NTDs.16",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Strive to reach a healthy weight before trying to get pregnant.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Talk to your health care provider about what a healthy weight is for you and about a plan to help you achieve it.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Learn your family’s health history.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Your health care provider will ask for information about your family’s genetic and health history. You may be referred for genetic counseling if certain conditions run in your family or if a family member was born with a physical abnormality or an intellectual and developmental disability. 13",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Get mentally healthy.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Good mental health means you feel good about your life and value yourself. It’s natural to worry or feel sad, anxious, or stressed at times. However, if these feelings do not go away and they interfere with your daily life, it’s important to seek help before you get pregnant.14 Hormonal changes and other situations during pregnancy can worsen depression.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Get mentally healthy.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Many people are familiar with the phrase “postpartum depression,” meaning depression that occurs after the birth of a baby. But we now know that it’s not just during the postpartum period, and it’s not just depression.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/preconceptioncare/conditioninfo/before-pregnancy",
    "title": "Can you promote a healthy pregnancy before getting pregnant? | NICHD - Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Get mentally healthy.",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Women experience depression and anxiety, as well as other mental health conditions, during pregnancy and after the baby is born. These conditions can have significant effects on the health of the mother and her child. Getting mentally healthy before you get pregnant can help minimize the effects of these conditions.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
