    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "general",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "If you experience symptoms of polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS), they'll usually become apparent in your late teens or early 20s.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "general",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Not all women with PCOS will have all of the symptoms, and each symptom can vary from mild to severe.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "general",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Some women only experience menstrual problems or are unable to conceive, or both.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "general",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "You should talk to your GP if you have any of these symptoms and think you may have PCOS.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Fertility problems",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "PCOS is one of the most common causes of female infertility. Many women discover they have PCOS when they're having difficulty getting pregnant.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Fertility problems",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "During each menstrual cycle, the ovaries release an egg (ovum) into the uterus (womb). This process is called ovulation and usually occurs once a month.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Fertility problems",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "But women with PCOS do not ovulate or ovulate infrequently, which means they have irregular or absent periods and find it difficult to get pregnant.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Having PCOS can increase your chances of developing other health problems in later life.",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "type 2 diabetes – a lifelong condition that causes a person's blood sugar level to become too high",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "depression and mood swings – because the symptoms of PCOS can affect your confidence and self-esteem",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "high blood pressure and high cholesterol – which can lead to heart disease and stroke",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "sleep apnoea – overweight women may also develop sleep apnoea, a condition that causes interrupted breathing during sleep",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Women who have had absent or very irregular periods (fewer than 3 or 4 periods a year) for many years have a higher than average risk of developing cancer of the womb lining (endometrial cancer).",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
  {
    "source": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/symptoms/",
    "title": "Polycystic ovary syndrome - Symptoms\n - NHS",
    "category": "clinical",
    "section": "Risks in later life",
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "But the chance of getting endometrial cancer is still small and can be minimised using treatments to regulate periods, such as the contraceptive pill or an intrauterine system (IUS).",
    "keyword": "Vaginitis"
  },
