      {
        "question": "What complications can arise from untreated vaginitis?",
        "answer": "Untreated vaginitis can lead to several complications depending on the type. Untreated bacterial vaginosis increases the risk of acquiring STIs (HIV, gonorrhea, chlamydia, HSV-2) by disrupting the protective vaginal flora; in pregnancy, it can cause preterm birth and postpartum infections. Untreated trichomoniasis increases HIV transmission risk 2-3 fold and is associated with pelvic inflammatory disease, infertility, and adverse pregnancy outcomes. Recurrent or untreated vulvovaginal candidiasis causes significant quality of life impairment and can indicate underlying immunosuppression or diabetes. Untreated atrophic vaginitis leads to progressive vaginal stenosis, painful intercourse, and recurrent urinary tract infections. In all types, chronic inflammation increases susceptibility to other infections."
